  "title": "Pesticide Exposure and ALS Risk: What a Major Study Reveals About a Possible Environmental Link",
  "summary": "New research explores the connection between pesticides and ALS A major scientific review has raised fresh concerns about the possible connection between pesticide exposure and Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis (ALS), a devastating neurological disease that gradually destroys the nerve cells responsible for movement. The study suggests that people who regularly work with pesticides may face a significantly higher risk of developing ALS compared with those who have little or no exposure. Researcher",
